---
description: Headroom context compression (manual start only)
alwaysApply: true
---

Headroom is **stopped** and **will not auto-start**. Graphify still works locally.

## Start Headroom manually (when you want it)

```bash
headroom proxy --memory              # foreground; Ctrl+C to stop
headroom doctor                      # verify it is running
```

## Do not auto-start again unless you choose to

```bash
# This re-enables boot + cron auto-start — only run if you want that:
headroom deploy --providers manual --target cursor --memory --no-docker
```

## With graphify

1. `graphify query "<question>"` first
2. Read only lines you will edit
3. `graphify update .` after code changes

**Note:** Cursor cannot use `127.0.0.1` Headroom (cloud blocks private networks). Use normal Cursor models, or expose Headroom via a public tunnel if needed.
